<title>USA: MBIA qualifies 13 issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>MBIA qualifies 13 issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>MBIA Insurance Corp said it has qualified for bond insurance the following 13 municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>--Central Union High School, Calif., General Obligations (GOs), $5.15 million.</p>
<p>--San Juan Capistrano, Calif., $1.8 million taxables as a direct purchase.</p>
<p>--University of Kentucky, $6.645 million revenue bonds.</p>
<p>--Quincy, Mass., GOs., $12.335 million.</p>
<p>--Eden Prairie, Minn., $2.865 million refunding improvement GOs and $3.105 million refunding GOs.</p>
<p>--Hopkins, Minn., $1.7 million GO improvement (tax).</p>
<p>--Shakopee, Minn., GOs, $3.14 million.</p>
<p>--St Louis County Housing Redevelopment, Minn., $5.275 million revenue bonds.</p>
<p>--Bolivar-Richburg Central School District, N.Y., GOs, $2.865 million.</p>
<p>--Westbury, UFSD, N.Y., $3 million.</p>
<p>--Charleston, S.C., $5.2 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Hamilton County, Tenn., $53 million GOs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
